('286', '15', '_process_steps', 'field_svc_process'),
('287', '15', 'service_faq', 'a:12:{i:0;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:47:"How much should I spend on Google Ads in Dubai?";s:6:"answer";s:512:"The right Google Ads budget depends on your industry, target keywords, and growth goals. As a starting point, you need enough budget to gather meaningful conversion data — typically a minimum of AED 5,000–10,000/month for most Dubai industries. Highly competitive sectors like real estate or legal require significantly more to be competitive. We\'ll recommend a specific budget range based on your keyword CPCs, conversion rate benchmarks for your industry, and the volume of leads or sales you\'re targeting.";}i:1;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:46:"What is a good ROAS for Google Ads in the UAE?";s:6:"answer";s:474:"Average ROAS varies significantly by industry and campaign type. E-commerce businesses typically target 3–6x ROAS (for every AED 1 spent, generating AED 3–6 in revenue). Lead generation businesses use cost per lead as the primary metric instead. Our managed portfolio averages 4.2x ROAS, but the right target for your business depends on your margins, customer lifetime value, and acquisition cost tolerance. We\'ll establish a custom target based on your unit economics.";}i:2;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:54:"How long does it take for Google Ads to start working?";s:6:"answer";s:451:"Google Ads can generate leads or sales from day one of launching — unlike SEO, which takes months to show results. However, campaigns typically improve significantly in the first 4–8 weeks as Smart Bidding algorithms learn and as we make optimisation improvements based on initial data. Expect the first 2–4 weeks to be a learning phase, with meaningful efficiency improvements in weeks 4–12 and continued compounding optimisation beyond that.";}i:3;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:58:"Should I use Google Ads or Meta Ads for my Dubai business?";s:6:"answer";s:539:"The answer is usually both — but with different objectives. Google Ads is ideal for capturing existing demand (people actively searching for what you offer). Meta Ads is ideal for creating demand (reaching people who match your ideal customer profile but aren\'t actively searching right now). B2C brands with visual products and broad audiences often see strong results from Meta. B2B and high-intent service businesses typically see better lead quality from Google Search. We\'ll recommend the right mix based on your specific situation.";}i:4;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:45:"What is Quality Score and why does it matter?";s:6:"answer";s:449:"Quality Score is Google\'s 1–10 rating of your keyword-ad-landing page relevance and expected performance. A higher Quality Score means Google rewards you with lower CPCs — a QS 10 keyword can cost 50% less per click than a QS 5 keyword for the same ad position. We actively manage Quality Scores by ensuring tight keyword-to-ad-copy relevance, improving expected CTR through ad copy testing, and optimising landing page relevance and experience.";}i:5;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:51:"Do you manage PPC for e-commerce businesses in UAE?";s:6:"answer";s:409:"Yes, and it\'s one of our strongest specialisms. E-commerce PPC requires Google Shopping expertise (product feed optimisation, campaign structure, Performance Max configuration), Dynamic Search Ads, and remarketing campaigns targeting cart abandoners and past purchasers. We\'ve delivered strong ROAS improvements for UAE e-commerce brands across fashion, electronics, beauty, home goods, and consumer products.";}i:6;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:63:"Can you take over management of an existing Google Ads account?";s:6:"answer";s:401:"Yes. We take over existing accounts regularly. We start with a comprehensive audit to understand the account\'s history, identify immediate quick wins, and flag structural issues. We then implement changes systematically — not all at once, as dramatic changes to a well-trained Smart Bidding account can disrupt performance. The transition is managed carefully to minimise any performance disruption.";}i:7;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:59:"How do you prevent click fraud in UAE Google Ads campaigns?";s:6:"answer";s:407:"Google has its own click fraud protection built in, but for campaigns in competitive UAE markets we also recommend and implement third-party click fraud protection (such as ClickCease or TrafficGuard) that provides more granular filtering. We also monitor traffic quality metrics regularly — bounce rate, time on site, conversion rate by source — to identify and exclude any suspicious traffic patterns.";}i:8;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:50:"What reporting will I receive on my PPC campaigns?";s:6:"answer";s:425:"You\'ll receive a comprehensive monthly performance report covering all key metrics: impressions, clicks, CTR, average CPC, conversions, conversion rate, cost per conversion, and ROAS. We also provide a live dashboard (Google Looker Studio) for real-time access to your campaign data. Monthly strategy calls review performance, discuss learnings, and align on the next month\'s priorities. Full transparency — no black boxes.";}i:9;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:45:"Do you offer PPC management for LinkedIn Ads?";s:6:"answer";s:404:"Yes. LinkedIn Ads is particularly effective for B2B UAE businesses targeting decision-makers by job title, seniority, industry, and company size. While LinkedIn CPCs are higher than Google or Meta, the lead quality and targeting precision for high-value B2B offers makes it extremely cost-effective for the right business type. We run LinkedIn Sponsored Content, Message Ads, and Lead Gen Form campaigns.";}i:10;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:58:"What happens to my ad accounts if I stop working with you?";s:6:"answer";s:401:"You retain full ownership of all ad accounts — always. If you end the engagement, we provide a full handover including account documentation, campaign structure explanation, and recommendations for the new manager. Your ad history, conversion data, and audience lists remain yours. We won\'t hold your accounts hostage or create dependency — your success is our success, and we operate accordingly.";}i:11;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:57:"How do you handle PPC for seasonal businesses in the UAE?";s:6:"answer";s:499:"Seasonality in the UAE is significant — Ramadan, summer slowdowns, the peak season October–March, and major events like Expo and DSF all affect search volumes and consumer behaviour. We plan campaign strategies around the UAE calendar: scaling budgets during peak periods, running awareness campaigns during slower periods to build pipeline for the next peak, and adjusting bid strategies and messaging for seasonal events. Proactive seasonal planning rather than reactive adjustment is the key.";}}'),
