('303', '18', 'service_faq', 'a:12:{i:0;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:51:"What web development technologies do you work with?";s:6:"answer";s:374:"Our team covers a broad range: WordPress (our primary CMS platform), React and Next.js for modern JavaScript applications, Vue.js, PHP and Laravel for backend development, Node.js for API services, WooCommerce for e-commerce, and headless CMS architectures. We select the technology that best fits your requirements rather than forcing every project into a single framework.";}i:1;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:35:"How long does web development take?";s:6:"answer";s:415:"Development timelines depend on project scope. A standard WordPress business website (10–15 pages) takes 4–6 weeks of development after designs are approved. A WooCommerce store with custom functionality takes 6–10 weeks. A complex web application or custom platform takes 12–24+ weeks. We provide detailed project timelines in proposals, and we use iterative sprints so you see working progress throughout.";}i:2;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:43:"What does "Core Web Vitals optimised" mean?";s:6:"answer";s:401:"Core Web Vitals are Google\'s speed and experience metrics: LCP (how fast the main content loads), INP (how quickly the page responds to user interaction), and CLS (how stable the layout is while loading). Google uses these as ranking factors. A site that passes Core Web Vitals has a structural ranking advantage over slower competitors. We build to pass these from day one — not as an afterthought.";}i:3;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:43:"Do you integrate with UAE payment gateways?";s:6:"answer";s:341:"Yes. We integrate with all major UAE payment gateways: PayTabs, Telr, HyperPay, Amazon Payment Services (formerly Payfort), Network International, and international gateways like Stripe that operate in the UAE. We also implement Apple Pay, Google Pay, and credit/debit card processing in compliance with UAE banking and PCI DSS requirements.";}i:4;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:51:"Do you build websites with Arabic language support?";s:6:"answer";s:367:"Yes, including full RTL (right-to-left) layout support. Arabic web development is more than translation — it requires mirrored page layouts, proper Arabic font rendering, bidirectional text handling, and culturally adapted UX patterns. We\'ve built fully bilingual Arabic/English websites and applications, with language switching that works seamlessly for the user.";}i:5;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:35:"How do you ensure website security?";s:6:"answer";s:438:"Our security practices include: HTTPS with modern TLS, input validation and parameterised queries to prevent SQL injection, XSS protection, CSRF tokens on forms, secure file upload handling, rate limiting, regular dependency updates, and for WordPress — login protection, file permission hardening, and activity monitoring. We also recommend and configure Cloudflare as a WAF (web application firewall) for an additional security layer.";}i:6;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:39:"Can you build a custom web application?";s:6:"answer";s:335:"Yes. We build custom web applications for complex business requirements: customer portals, booking systems, SaaS applications, internal operations dashboards, marketplace platforms, and API-driven systems. We use modern frameworks (React/Next.js for frontend, Node.js or Laravel for backend) and architect for scalability from day one.";}i:7;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:45:"Do you offer website maintenance and support?";s:6:"answer";s:372:"Yes. We offer monthly maintenance plans that cover WordPress core, plugin, and theme updates; security monitoring and patching; regular backups (daily, stored offsite); uptime monitoring with alerting; and a monthly performance check. Maintenance is essential for keeping WordPress sites secure and performing well — outdated plugins are the #1 cause of WordPress hacks.";}i:8;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:50:"Can you fix or optimise our existing slow website?";s:6:"answer";s:386:"Yes. We offer standalone performance optimisation services: a comprehensive audit identifying the causes of slow performance, followed by implementation of fixes — server configuration improvements, caching, image optimisation, JavaScript/CSS optimisation, CDN setup, and database query optimisation. Most websites see significant measurable improvement in LCP and overall load times.";}i:9;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:67:"What happens to the website and code after the project is finished?";s:6:"answer";s:376:"You own everything. All code is yours — we transfer full repository access at project completion. All server access, domain, and hosting accounts are in your name from day one. Full project documentation is provided at handover. We have no interest in creating lock-in or dependency — our goal is to hand you a website you can manage, maintain, and build on independently.";}i:10;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:35:"Do you develop mobile applications?";s:6:"answer";s:347:"We develop Progressive Web Apps (PWAs) — web applications that behave like native mobile apps and can be installed on home screens — as part of our web development service. For native iOS and Android apps (React Native or Flutter), we partner with specialist mobile development teams. We can advise on the right approach for your requirements.";}i:11;a:2:{s:8:"question";s:45:"How do you handle hosting for UAE businesses?";s:6:"answer";s:415:"We recommend and configure hosting but you retain full account ownership. For most UAE business websites we recommend managed WordPress hosting (Kinsta, WP Engine, or Cloudways on a UAE/EU server) with Cloudflare CDN. For enterprise applications or data-residency requirements, we architect on Azure UAE North or AWS Bahrain. We\'re platform-agnostic — we configure whatever best fits your requirements and budget.";}}'),
